{# The control under a table of the account that is longer than one page (architecture §5.2): which rows of
   the whole list the reader is looking at, and the way to the page before it and the page after it.

   It is rendered only where there is more than one page, a control that can do nothing being a control
   nobody should have to read. The page it names is the "page" of the query string, which is the one word
   every table of this plane is paged by (AskedPage), and a link it writes keeps whatever else the request
   carried: the page of one application is read at an address that names that application.

   A page before the first or after the last is not a link but the same words unlinked, so that what a
   reader may do and what they may not are read in one place and in one shape.

   The bundle ships the shape and the words, never a class: "data-pager" is what a stylesheet reads.
   Overridable by an application under templates/bundles/BeffroiBundle/. #}
{% trans_default_domain 'beffroi' %}
{% if listing.pages > 1 %}
    {% set route = app.request.attributes.get('_route') %}
    {% set parameters = (app.request.attributes.get('_route_params') ?? {})|merge(app.request.query.all) %}
    <nav data-pager="{{ listing.pagination.number }}" data-pages="{{ listing.pages }}" aria-label="{{ 'pager.pages'|trans }}">
        <p data-pager-rows>{{ 'pager.rows'|trans({first: listing.firstRow, last: listing.lastRow, total: listing.total}) }}</p>
        {% if listing.hasPrevious %}
            <a href="{{ path(route, parameters|merge({page: listing.previous})) }}" data-pager="previous" rel="prev">{{ 'pager.previous'|trans }}</a>
        {% else %}
            <span data-pager="previous" aria-disabled="true">{{ 'pager.previous'|trans }}</span>
        {% endif %}
        {% if listing.hasNext %}
            <a href="{{ path(route, parameters|merge({page: listing.next})) }}" data-pager="next" rel="next">{{ 'pager.next'|trans }}</a>
        {% else %}
            <span data-pager="next" aria-disabled="true">{{ 'pager.next'|trans }}</span>
        {% endif %}
    </nav>
{% endif %}
